    "lawCode": "Amd §410.10, CP L; add §209, amd §274, Cor L; add §259-t, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Criminal Procedure Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S2803\n\nSPONSOR: BAILEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the criminal procedure law, the correction law, and the\nexecutive law, in relation to bona fide work not being considered a\nparole violation\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to allow re-entry workers the ability to\nwork overtime and night shifts.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThe first section of the bill amends section 410.10 of the criminal\nprocedure law by adding a new subdivision requiring courts to expressly\nstate it shall not be considered a violation if a re-entry worker\nengages in bona fide work and travel during curfew times.\n\nSection 2 amends the correction law by adding a new section 209 allowing\nreentry workers to engage in bona fide work and travel during curfew\ntimes in cases where the individual has been granted presumptive\nrelease, parole, conditional release, or release to post-release super-\nvision.\n\nSection 3 amends section 274 of the correction law by adding a new\nsubdivision prohibiting local conditional release commissions across the\nstate from violating re-entry workers for engaging in bona fide work and\ntravel during curfew times.\n\nSection 4 amends the executive law by adding a new section 259-t prohib-\niting the state board of parole from terminating presumptive release,\nparole, conditional release, release to post-release supervision, or any\nother type of supervised release solely because a re-entry worker\nengaged in bona fide work or travel during curfew times.\n\nSection 5 sets for forth the effective date.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nThe law allows for the imposition of special conditions without regard\nfor those who need some flexibility in terms of work schedules, work\nhours, or travel.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nEngaging in bona fide work is essential for re-entry workers to reinte-\ngrate into society and provide for their families. This bill will ensure\nthat reentry workers will not face any barriers to entering or re-enter-\ning the workforce solely because the state wishes to impose arbitrary\ntime restrictions.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT ON THE STATE:\n\nNone.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n2019-20: S7899/A10788 - Referred to Codes\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
